1
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:09,750
Three visionary tales. One unforgettable place.

2
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:13,500
The House is a animation, drama, comedy film directed by Paloma Baeza.

3
00:18:11,250 --> 00:18:17,250
Across different eras, a poor family, an anxious developer and a fed-up landlady
become tied to the same mysterious house in this animated dark comedy.

4
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:21,000
Mabel (voice), played by Mia Goth.

5
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:24,750
Raymond (voice), played by Matthew Goode.

6
00:36:22,500 --> 00:36:28,500
Penelope (voice), played by Claudie Blakley.

7
00:42:26,250 --> 00:42:32,250
Isobel (voice), played by Eleanor De Swaef-Roels.

8
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
Mr. Thomas (voice), played by Mark Heap.

9
00:54:33,750 --> 00:54:39,750
Great Aunt Eleanor (voice), played by Stephanie Cole.

10
01:00:37,500 --> 01:00:43,500
The House is a 2022 British stop-motion adult animated
anthology television special created by Enda Walsh.

11
01:06:41,250 --> 01:06:47,250
The production is divided into three chapters telling different stories spanning different worlds, interior designs, and characters (consisting of humans,
anthropomorphic rodents and insects, and felines) in the same house; each story deals with themes of madness, wealth, and the pursuit of true happiness.

12
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:51,000
Originally announced as an anthology miniseries, owing to its
short length, it became a television special.

13
01:18:48,750 --> 01:18:54,750
Produced for Netflix by Nexus Studios in London, it tells three chapters respectively directed by the duo of Emma de Swaef and Marc James Roels, Niki Lindroth von
Bahr, and Paloma Baeza; the directors are credited with the story of their respective segments, with Johannes Nyholm as co-writer for the second.

14
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:58,500
The film explores themes of dark comedy, surreal, stop motion.

15
01:30:56,250 --> 01:31:02,250
The tone is lighthearted and dark and emotional.
